<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21252" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭālysus-</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰάλυσος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A son of the fourth Sol</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 21, 54</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a famous picture of him by Protogenes, at
					Rhodes, afterwards in Rome,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 60, § 135</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Or. 2, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35, 10, 36, § 102</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Gell. 15, 31,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			f., <i>an ancient city of Rhodes</i>, now
			the <i>village of Ialiso</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 31, 35, §
			132</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭālysĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				lalysus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Telchines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 365</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
